WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:19.770
A couple of weeks ago, we uploaded a video
all about microbes in slow motion, but here’s

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:24.700
the thing about recording in slow motion,
when you record for a minute, you end up with

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.260
way more than a minute of video, because it
is in slow motion.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:33.340
So you end up with a lot more footage than
you need for an average episode of Journey

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:34.449
to the Microcosmos.

00:00:34.449 --> 00:00:38.820
And this week, we’re taking a break from
our normal uploads in order to give our team

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:44.010
some time to relax during the holiday break,
but we also wanted to give you a chance to

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:50.869
sit back, relax, take a break from whatever’s
going on, and enjoy all of the uncut footage

00:00:50.869 --> 00:00:52.170
from our slow motion video.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:56.729
Now, if you’re looking for more information
about the clips in this video, be sure to

00:00:56.729 --> 00:01:01.909
go back and check out our Microbes in Slow
Motion video because today, we’ll only be

00:01:01.909 --> 00:01:07.320
featuring our Master of Microscopes James
Weiss’s beautiful images and Andrew Huang’s

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:13.330
fantastic music and I am going to stop talking
and let you enjoy those in just a second.

00:01:13.330 --> 00:01:18.901
But before I go, I should mention that if
you do enjoy this type of thing, we upload

00:01:18.901 --> 00:01:23.430
an hour long video like this every month for
our patrons over at Patreon.com/journeytomicro.

00:01:23.430 --> 00:35:02.619
Alright, that’s all, enjoy!

